CM_ "RG-01 wire draft. Model, blending and vehicle runtime are separate. See docs/interfaces/drive-frame.md.";
CM_ BO_ 386 "Standard 11-bit CAN FD, DLC 13 (32 bytes), 10 ms logical period. BRS=0, ESI=0.";
CM_ BO_ 642 "DLC 15 (64 bytes). Independent actual torque plus wheel speed and regenerative capability. Not command echo.";
CM_ SG_ 386 Torque "Aggregate driven-wheel demand: positive propulsion, negative forward regenerative braking, valid 0 no torque demand. Raw -32768 reserved invalid. Scaling/range are project wire choices, not OEM calibration.";
CM_ SG_ 642 Torque "Independent actual driven-wheel motor torque after dynamics and local protection. Raw -32768 invalid. Torque validity is independent from auxiliary feedback usability.";
CM_ SG_ 642 WheelSpeed "Nonnegative forward equivalent wheel speed. Raw 65535 invalid; invalid flag requires sentinel and zero source timestamp.";
CM_ SG_ 642 RegenTorqueLimit "Nonnegative regenerative torque magnitude. Valid 0 means unavailable regeneration, not invalid information. Raw 65535 invalid; raw 32768..65534 forbidden.";
CM_ SG_ 642 RegenCapabilityValid "Separate from torque validity. Valid capability requires usable wheel speed and source/input freshness. Invalid flag requires sentinel, InputsInvalid reason and zero capability timestamps.";
CM_ SG_ 642 RegenLimitReason "Diagnostic reason, not permission to use a stale limit. Disabled requires valid zero limit; invalid capability uses InputsInvalid.";
CM_ SG_ 386 SourceTimeNs "Zone allocation generation time in common Epoch/CLOCK_MONOTONIC domain.";
CM_ SG_ 642 SourceTimeNs "Valid torque: original acquisition time, including asynchronous samples. Unavailable torque: diagnostic generation time. Cached torque cannot refresh valid RX. ADR-0036, 2026-10-18; schema/layout unchanged.";
CM_ SG_ 642 WheelSpeedSourceTimeNs "Original independent wheel speed source. May follow torque acquisition; bounded by receiver now/session and its own age/cursor. Never replace with frame transmission time.";
CM_ SG_ 642 CapabilitySourceTimeNs "Independent capability calculation time, retained on cache reuse. May follow torque acquisition; bounded by receiver now/session and its own age/cursor.";
CM_ SG_ 642 CapabilityInputTimeNs "Oldest source time of every dependency used by capability calculation, including wheel speed and charge acceptance. New calculation time cannot rejuvenate stale input.";
CM_ SG_ 386 E2ECrc "AUTOSAR P05, DataID 0x1201 low/high. Cover bytes 0..28 and 31. CRC LE at 29..30, Counter at 31.";
CM_ SG_ 642 E2ECrc "P05 DataID 0x1202. Cover bytes 0..28 AND 31..63, then DataID low/high. Entire capability extension is protected.";
CM_ SG_ 386 E2ECounter "Independent command Protect state; wraps 255 to 0. Not application Sequence.";
CM_ SG_ 642 E2ECounter "Independent actual Protect state, including capability extension.";
CM_ SG_ 386 CausalSequence "Upstream vehicle command sequence in common Epoch.";
CM_ SG_ 642 CausalSequence "Last accepted DriveCommand sequence; ignored for NoAcceptedInput.";

